# Issue: 
Adjust Medicine alert to check current date (in addition to current time) and connect to retrieve actual user's medicine info instead of getting the test user data.

# Solution: 
Changed MedicineToast to use React functional components and useEffect React hook. The medication time is now checked every 10 seconds from the corresponding logged in user's data (before was checking a dummy user account). The MedicineToast code uses useAuthContext to the userID and fetched data from Firebase using data references and snapshots.

# Testing: 
Toast appears as expected when the current time and day matches the medicine time and day that's stored in the Firebase database. See image below. On the right hand side, we can see the user's (me) medicine information stored in Firebase.  Since the current day/time and the medicine day/time matches, a toast appears reminding the user to take XYZ medicine.

To test it locally on your machine, go to MedicineToast.jsx and find the lines...
// For testing purposes, uncomment the code below and adjust to match 
// your medicine day and medicine time 
// const currentDay = "friday";
// const currentTime = "05:54";
Change currentDay and currentTime to match the medicine day and medicine time associated with your user account. Also, comment out the existing code that initializes currentDay and currentTime.

